1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:07,560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

2
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:12,980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

3
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:22,860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

4
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:25,540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

5
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:31,840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

6
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:37,960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

7
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:44,040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

8
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:50,200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

9
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:57,080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

10
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:02,620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

11
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:09,340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

12
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:15,100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

13
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:21,300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

14
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:28,120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

15
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:32,820
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

16
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,240
Hello, Edward.

17
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:36,820
You appear to have grown some.

18
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,420
I spoke with Pinako.

19
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,300
- You tried human transmutation.
- [GASP]

20
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:48,080
What makes you think
you can show up like this?

21
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,800
There's nothing left
for you here anymore!

22
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:53,580
I noticed.

23
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,640
Tell me, Edward...

24
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,300
what possessed you
to burn down my home?

25
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:02,500
After what happened
we vowed to never turn back.

26
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,920
- We did it as a symbol of our resolve.
- No you didn't.

27
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,540
- You were hiding the memory.
- [GASP]

28
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:12,880
You didn't want to be reminded
of what you've done,

29
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,760
and thought you could erase the
memory by destroying the evidence.

30
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,800
You're wrong!

31
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:23,680
It's just like a child who hides
the sheets after he wets the bed.

32
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,720
You ran away, and you know it.

33
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,780
[SHUDDERING GASP]

34
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,020
I...

35
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:33,020
You don't know a damn thing!

36
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:36,300
You make me sick to my stomach.

37
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:41,960
He's exactly like I was when I was his age.

38
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:52,220
[DOOR OPENS]

39
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:59,540
[YOUNG ED AND AL LAUGHING]

40
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,560
[DOOR CLOSES]

41
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:25,960
[LOW GROWLING]

42
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,260
PINAKO: You haven't changed
in the slightest.

43
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:30,540
All these years...

44
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:33,300
and you look exactly the same.
[CHUCKLES]

45
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:38,340
Where have you been all this time?
Why didn't you come back sooner?

46
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:41,080
Tricia was waiting for you
until the very end.

47
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,100
- Pinako
- Hm?

48
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:55,340
The life form my sons transmuted...

49
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:59,320
- are you positive that it was Tricia?
- Huh?

50
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,040
Well, I wouldn't...

51
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:04,840
it didn't even look human to me...

52
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:08,140
- so I wouldn't think of it as—
- No. That's not what I'm asking.

53
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:12,780
Did you notice the eye color,
or the hair color?

54
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,420
Huh?

55
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,200
What are you trying to get at?

56
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:20,160
Are you telling me that
that wasn't even Tricia?

57
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,660
For all that those boys sacrificed...

58
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:28,160
you're saying that thing they created
wasn't even their mother?

59
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:33,760
LING: Whoa, you don't sleep or eat? 
You don't even run out of breath?

60
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:37,260
AL: Uh-huh, I just have to make
sure the seal doesn't get harmed.

61
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:38,900
That's so cool!

62
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,920
So you really are immortal then, huh?

63
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,160
- No, I'm not.
-[GASPS]

64
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:46,500
This body, it's like a time bomb.

65
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,280
Barry mentioned something,

66
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:53,920
and it made me realize that any type of body
is incompatible with a foreign soul.

67
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:58,000
Pairing them together,
the body will eventually reject it.

68
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,580
[GASP]

69
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:04,340
It could happen tomorrow, or ten years
from now, but it's inevitable that it will.

70
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:05,780
Oh no!

71
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:08,640
Al, we've got to get you
back in your regular body!

72
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:10,000
LING: Well, hold on.

73
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,440
If it's about to give out on you...

74
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:15,720
couldn't you just transfer your soul
into some other object?

75
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:18,060
Because if that's the case...

76
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,640
then for the time being...

77
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:22,660
well you're impervious to pain,
and you don't have to eat!

78
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:25,480
It sounds like a great deal to me!

79
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:26,540
No it isn't!

80
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,840
You don't know what you're talking about!

81
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:33,280
Sorry.

82
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:35,480
Winry?!

83
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,120
[DOOR CLOSES]

84
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,500
[KNOCKING]

85
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:48,100
AL: Winry?
I'm coming in.

86
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:59,160
You know, you and brother
always gotta be the first to explode.

87
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:02,040
I never get the chance
to be the one to get mad.

88
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:06,120
It's just... Well...

89
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,200
I guess I can't fall asleep.

90
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,280
I don't think this body will let me.

91
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:16,680
Oh.

92
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:27,160
Just tell me you're going
to get your body back.

93
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:28,900
Okay?

94
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:30,840
[AL GASPS]

95
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:35,860
ED: Give it back!

96
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:38,180
You have to give my brother his body back!

97
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:40,080
He's the only family I have!

98
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:42,240
I won't let you take it!

99
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:43,220
Take it?

100
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,660
- [ED GASPS]
- Do you even know what you're saying?

101
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:49,100
You're the one who tossed his body aside
and put him in that armor.

102
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:51,460
- Aren't you, Alchemist?
-[ED GASPS]

103
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,060
It's true.

104
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:56,220
You and I are exactly the same.

105
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:58,080
Accept it, Edward.

106
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,760
- We make monsters.

107
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:02,100
[GASP]

108
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:04,980
[DISORTED VOICE] Edward...

109
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:08,180
Why did you leave me here like this?

110
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,180
[SHUDDERING GASP]

111
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:13,660
PINAKO: Ed? Get out of bed already!

112
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:15,620
Your father's about to head out!

113
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:19,040
[WHIMPERING]

114
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:22,520
This one.

115
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:24,040
Do you mind if I keep it?

116
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:27,660
It's the only photo we had
taken with all four of us.

117
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:29,560
Of course. You're welcome to it.

118
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:30,660
Thank you.

119
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,240
I need to tell you
something important, Pinako.

120
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,560
Huh?

121
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,800
[DOOR OPENS]

122
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:43,620
Something terrible is going
to happen in this country soon.

123
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,780
You should escape while you can.

124
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:46,800
[SCOFFS]

125
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:49,540
This country's lousy with terrible things.

126
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:51,380
And I can't leave.

127
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:54,940
I've got other people who need me
here in case they want to come home.

128
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:58,680
I've given you my warning.

129
00:08:01,340 --> 00:08:02,980
Hey, Hohenheim, wait!

130
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,260
Try not to be such a stranger, all right?

131
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:13,600
I wish I could, Pinako.

132
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:16,980
It's too bad I won't get to
enjoy your cooking anymore.

133
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:25,900
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

134
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:43,780
You're not really gonna dig it up,
are you, Ed?

135
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:46,700
[SHOVEL CLANGS, ED GRUNTS]

136
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,160
Why don't we go back?

137
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:52,840
No.

138
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,520
My stumps are aching from the weather.

139
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,000
It's about to rain.

140
00:08:57,540 --> 00:08:59,140
Let's just hurry and do this.

141
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:16,160
[ED GAGGING]

142
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,560
Ed!

143
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Don't push yourself.

144
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:26,000
[SHUDDERING AND GROANING]

145
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,900
Let's head on home.

146
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,440
No.

147
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,240
[SHUDDERS]

148
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,760
I'm not gonna be able to move
forward until I know for sure.

149
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,560
Besides...

150
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,000
You ran away.

151
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:43,200
I won't run away from this.

152
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,020
[SHOVEL HITS BONE]

153
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:36,920
[GASPS]

154
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:41,000
Granny...

155
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:45,000
Mom's hair was a light chestnut color...

156
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:48,080
This is black.

157
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:53,320
This femur, it's much too long.

158
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:58,680
And this pelvis, I'm pretty sure it's male.

159
00:10:58,820 --> 00:10:59,680
It is?

160
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:05,120
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
this isn't your mother, Ed.

161
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:09,440
[ED WHIMPERS]

162
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:22,380
[LAUGHING]

163
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,460
And that's it.

164
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:28,540
It really is impossible to
bring the dead back to life.

165
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,160
The undeniable truth.

166
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:35,780
[LAUGHS]
It was impossible all along

167
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:40,260
Edward, now listen to me.

168
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:42,440
You've gotta get a hold of yourself.

169
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,280
[SIGH]

170
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,680
I'm okay, Granny. It's okay.

171
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:52,380
From the moment I made this
thing, it's been a symbol of my despair.

172
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,260
But not anymore.

173
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:56,440
Now it's an emblem of hope.

174
00:11:58,060 --> 00:12:00,200
Al can be returned to normal!

175
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,300
Fullmetal Alchemist.

176
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,420
Fullmetal Alchemist.

177
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:24,300
[PHONE RINGING]

178
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,100
Curtis residence.

179
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:28,720
I didn't expect this.

180
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,040
You never call.

181
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:31,440
Uh, yeah.

182
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,000
I need to ask you something, teacher.

183
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,440
But, well...

184
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,320
Well what?

185
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:39,860
Spit it out.

186
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:45,620
It has to do with when you
tried to transmute your baby.

187
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:46,780
[GASP]

188
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,720
What about it, Ed?

189
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:54,740
The thing is... What Al and I transmuted...

190
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,840
It wasn't actually our mother.

191
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,220
What is this, Ed?

192
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:01,940
What are you trying to tell me?

193
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:05,900
I'm sorry to ask you this,
but the child you transmuted...

194
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:09,720
Are you sure that it was your
child that you brought back?

195
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:12,580
[GASP]

196
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:14,580
[PHONE HANGS UP]

197
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:23,860
PINAKO: Thank you, Ed.

198
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:28,040
It's good to know my son
and his wife helped people.

199
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:31,360
I'm proud of them.

200
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,640
So Hohenheim...

201
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,900
Did he even bother to say where he was going?

202
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,720
Of course he didn't.

203
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:46,640
And I didn't a—

204
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,840
Ahh!

205
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,280
What's wrong with me?

206
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:52,080
I can't believe I forgot
to give him the message!

207
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:53,580
A message?

208
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:54,600
Yes.

209
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:57,960
A last request...
From your mother.

210
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,400
I'll be gone when he returns.

211
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,040
Can you tell him something?

212
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:08,300
I need him to know... I
couldn't keep my promise.

213
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:10,220
I died before he did.

214
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:12,280
And I'm so sorry.

215
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,660
Promise?

216
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:15,460
What promise?

217
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:16,920
You got me.

218
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:20,620
Sorry to ask, but could you
pass it on if you bump into him?

219
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,440
Why should I have to?

220
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:26,960
I know it doesn't seem like it,
but he does care about you and your brother.

221
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,100
[LAUGHS]

222
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:31,400
Yeah, I'll pass it on right
after I clock him in the face.

223
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:33,400
[TRAIN HORN]

224
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,660
Heading back to Central
already, are you?

225
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:42,620
Yeah. Al's probably mad at me.
I'm gonna have plenty of explaining to do.

226
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:49,340
What the hell?!

227
00:14:49,380 --> 00:14:51,140
I'm sorry, brother!

228
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:54,240
Wha—how are you this beat up?!

229
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,000
And you!

230
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,120
What the hell are you doing here?!

231
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:00,760
Eating a delicious dinner.

232
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:02,000
[DOOR OPENS]

233
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:04,120
Seriously!

234
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:05,920
How did this happen to you?!

235
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:06,940
Uh...

236
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:11,160
ED: A Homunculus
and Barry the Chopper...

237
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:15,380
And just to throw a cherry on top,
you find out your body might reject your soul.

238
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:20,940
I'm gonna have to extend what
little you have left of your armor.

239
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,060
[SIGHS]

240
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,700
Ed, he'll be able to get
his body back, right?

241
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:38,160
Yeah, of course he will.

242
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:40,420
I told you I'm gonna get it back.

243
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,460
Al...

244
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:47,980
I've gotta tell you something.

245
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,900
I dug up the body that we
transmuted in Resembool.

246
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:51,000
[AL GASPS]

247
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:54,860
What?!

248
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:56,240
Why would you do that?!

249
00:15:56,260 --> 00:15:57,460
Because, Al...

250
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:01,220
I found out that the thing we buried
wasn't really our mother.

251
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:03,740
[GASP]

252
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:07,740
But... Hold on a minute.

253
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:09,120
The thing we made?
Then that means...

254
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,620
The thing we made?

255
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:13,300
I don't know what,
but it was something completely different.

256
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:16,100
But if it wasn't, then what happened to me?

257
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,200
That's just it.

258
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:20,180
This has actually convinced
me we can return you to normal.

259
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:20,960
[AL GASPS]

260
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,060
Ed, are you sure?

261
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:22,880
Yeah.

262
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:26,180
But before I start explaining how...

263
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:29,880
Well, uh, Winry... Do, um... Uh...

264
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:33,800
Do you remember when Al and I got in a fight
when we were kids about...

265
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,000
Who'd marry you?

266
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:35,780
Huh?

267
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,100
The fight we were
talking about on the roof?

268
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:39,280
Yeah, that one.

269
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:41,300
Al told me you turned him down.

270
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,020
Mm-hmm.

271
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:43,200
Turned you both down.

272
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,200
Whatever.

273
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,040
So the question's for both of you, then.

274
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,700
What was your reasoning?

275
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:49,740
She said...

276
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,760
[BOTH]: "I just don't like
men who are shorter than me."

277
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,760
[ED SCREAMS]

278
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,960
You can't judge a man
for something he can't help!

279
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:00,020
WINRY: Uh...
ED: [WAILING]

280
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:03,760
WINRY: I don't really see how this has anything to do with getting Al's body back.
ED: [CONTINUES WAILING]

281
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,460
I had to be sure.

282
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:08,200
Al had a memory of
something I don't recall.

283
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:11,160
And you seem to clearly
remember it the same way, Winry.

284
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:13,760
Which means that it
happened without a doubt.

285
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:16,540
So now that we know you
remembered something real,

286
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:20,500
then we also know for a fact
that really is Al bonded in there.

287
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:23,100
I pulled you out, Al.

288
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:24,800
I actually did it.

289
00:17:25,180 --> 00:17:27,800
I know it was only your
soul, but that's just it...

290
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:30,760
If I was able to pull that much of you out,

291
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:34,760
then I've got a hunch that your body's
still in there, and I can pull it out.

292
00:17:35,020 --> 00:17:37,140
You think my body's still in the portal?

293
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:39,380
Existing separately from my soul?

294
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:42,120
[GASPS] Like Barry's body!

295
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:46,880
Right. What did you see?

296
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:48,100
Try to think back.

297
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:51,020
Can you remember what happened
when the truth unraveled you?

298
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,620
I reached out...

299
00:17:57,900 --> 00:17:59,260
And it was me.

300
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:01,040
It was my hand I grabbed!

301
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:02,820
I knew it.

302
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:05,200
Doesn't look like we're
done with the truth yet, Al.

303
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:07,640
We're gonna get in there
and pull your body out.

304
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:09,080
Brother...

305
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:14,100
AL: After the portal, I remember
looking at you from inside that thing...

306
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:16,360
The thing we thought was Mom.

307
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,980
You were inside of it?

308
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:20,760
That thing was you?

309
00:18:20,820 --> 00:18:22,000
AL: I guess so.

310
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,780
But my soul didn't bind.

311
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:25,920
It must have rejected me right away.

312
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,480
So that means...

313
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:31,460
We didn't harm
anyone else's soul after all.

314
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:34,260
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

315
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:35,280
[ED AND AL GASP]

316
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:39,020
Mr. Elric? You have
a telephone call from Izumi Curtis.

317
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:42,780
IZUMI: I did some research.

318
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:46,700
Sig and I looked up our family lines,
and well...

319
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:49,960
The child that I transmuted... It couldn't...

320
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:53,680
It didn't have a single physical trait
that could have come from us.

321
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:57,340
You're onto something, aren't you?

322
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:58,320
Yes.

323
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:01,280
I've come to the conclusion
that death is permanent.

324
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:05,800
So not even transmutation
can change that fact.

325
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,220
All this time...

326
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:11,980
I thought that I must have missed something.

327
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:14,700
But it was impossible
to do in the first place.

328
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:17,540
Ed.

329
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:18,760
Yes, ma'am?!

330
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,400
Thank you.
[LINE DISCONNECTS]

331
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,180
AL: So what did Teacher have to say?

332
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:32,660
Well, I'm not really sure why, but she said...

333
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:33,840
Thank you.

334
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:43,960
Al...?

335
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:49,840
This entire time, I've been
blaming myself for what happened.

336
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,720
I thought it was me.

337
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:56,420
I thought I was the one who
killed Mom a second time.

338
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,120
And so did I, Al.

339
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:03,660
Thanks, brother. Thank you.

340
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:06,920
I wasn't the one who killed Mom after all.

341
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:11,760
Izumi...

342
00:20:12,540 --> 00:20:15,040
I feel like I've been brought back to life.

343
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:19,520
Our child wasn't made to
suffer twice because of me.

344
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:23,460
ED: But still...

345
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:27,000
None of this changes the fact
that I'm the one who put you in that body.

346
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:30,480
And I don't care what it takes.
I'm gonna make you normal again—

347
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,220
Brother!

348
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:34,860
I was right there with you,
and I knew that there were risks.

349
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:38,040
So quit trying to shoulder
all of this on your own.

350
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:41,320
I can't watch you suffer like this.

351
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:43,020
Not on your own.

352
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:47,080
I can't just stand back and watch
other people get hurt over what I've done.

353
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:49,700
Like what happened to Mr. Hughes.

354
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:55,380
I felt like it was my fault
when I found out he was dead.

355
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:58,820
And I told myself that
if it meant other people getting hurt

356
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:01,140
then I don't even want my body back.

357
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,320
Brother...

358
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:09,560
I've met other people
who weren't exactly human.

359
00:21:09,780 --> 00:21:12,840
But they still managed to
live their lives with a purpose.

360
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:15,660
And even in this body...

361
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:19,320
it hasn't stopped other people
from treating me like I'm still human.

362
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:22,600
This body could reject me any time.

363
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:24,500
But it's the same with being human.

364
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:27,460
You never know when you
might get sick or die in an accident.

365
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,080
So I can still get by like this.

366
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:32,600
I can live a somewhat normal life.

367
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:35,160
And that's how I've managed to keep going.

368
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,980
But now...

369
00:21:37,340 --> 00:21:39,480
I can't take it anymore!

370
00:21:43,120 --> 00:21:46,840
Because... I can't...

371
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:50,600
I can't take all the nights by myself!

372
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:54,480
It's too lonely.

373
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:57,280
And that's why I have
to get back to normal.

374
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:59,860
Sure. And you're going to.

375
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:00,880
[CLANG]

376
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,600
We'll knock that truth jerk on his butt.

377
00:22:03,660 --> 00:22:06,360
And then we're gonna pull
your body right out of that place.

378
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,620
AL: Yeah!

379
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:18,720
WINRY: Huh?

380
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:21,700
That's weird.

381
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:25,280
Have his shoulders always been so broad?

382
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,400
Let it all out, let it all out

383
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

384
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

385
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

386
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

387
00:22:56,820 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

388
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

389
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

390
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:23,840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

391
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:31,780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

392
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

393
